// ============================================
// Detection: Excessive Failed Logins
// Source: Microsoft Sentinel Analytics Rule
// ============================================
//
// Description:
// This detection identifies multiple failed login attempts within a short time window.
// It is designed to detect potential brute force attacks or password spraying activity.
//
// Trigger Logic:
// - Monitors authentication logs (Entra ID Sign-in Logs)
// - Groups failed login attempts by user and IP address
// - Triggers when a defined threshold of failed attempts is exceeded within a time window
//
// Why This Matters:
// Repeated failed login attempts are a common indicator of:
// - Brute force attacks
// - Password spraying
// - Unauthorized access attempts
//
// Early detection helps prevent account compromise before a successful login occurs.
//
// Analyst Notes:
// - Investigate the targeted user account
// - Review the source IP address for reputation or unusual behavior
// - Check if the activity escalates into a successful login
// - Consider account lockout or enforcing MFA if not already enabled
//
// ============================================
let threshold = 5;
SigninLogs
| where ResultType != 0
| summarize FailedAttempts=count() 
    by UserPrincipalName, IPAddress, bin(TimeGenerated, 10m)
| where FailedAttempts >= threshold
// ============================================
